WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.099 --> 00:00:06.001
Dell has just updated their XPS 13 laptop
for 2019, and we got the entry-level i5 model

00:00:06.001 --> 00:00:14.040
for $1150, which is a great price considering
it packs 8GB of RAM and 256gigs of NVMe SSD

00:00:14.040 --> 00:00:15.040
storage.

00:00:15.040 --> 00:00:16.500
So let’s go through everything you need
to know about it.

00:00:16.500 --> 00:00:20.080
Just like last year, it’s encased in an
aluminum shell that looks and feels great

00:00:20.080 --> 00:00:22.270
compared to many other Windows laptops.

00:00:22.270 --> 00:00:26.150
The display has very thin great-looking bezels,
despite the fact that they’ve moved the

00:00:26.150 --> 00:00:28.760
webcam back up above the display.

00:00:28.760 --> 00:00:33.019
Last year’s model had the webcam under the
display to accommodate Windows Hello, a useful

00:00:33.019 --> 00:00:36.649
feature that scans your face to log you in
without having to enter your password.

00:00:36.649 --> 00:00:40.290
That feature is now gone, but it’s not a
big deal since the power button doubles as

00:00:40.290 --> 00:00:42.210
a fingerprint scanner for logging in.

00:00:42.210 --> 00:00:46.980
The display itself uses a 1080P panel that
definitely isn’t the sharpest display out

00:00:46.980 --> 00:00:51.840
there, but the excellent color accuracy and
matte filter make it one of the better 1080P

00:00:51.840 --> 00:00:52.930
displays you can find.

00:00:52.930 --> 00:00:56.570
But either way, if you care a lot about the
display, we’d recommend upgrading to the

00:00:56.570 --> 00:00:58.889
4K model for a few hundred dollars more.

00:00:58.889 --> 00:01:03.209
The keyboard feels pretty decent for a Windows
laptop with a good amount of travel.

00:01:03.209 --> 00:01:06.500
Typing is pretty comfortable, but some users
did complain that there was a bit too much

00:01:06.500 --> 00:01:08.189
spacing between the keys.

00:01:08.189 --> 00:01:12.970
Personally, we prefer the latest MacBook pro
keys which are wider and more clicky, but

00:01:12.970 --> 00:01:14.570
most people will prefer the Dells.

00:01:14.570 --> 00:01:18.860
It also features backlighting with two brightness
settings so it’s great for using at night.

00:01:18.860 --> 00:01:23.750
The build quality is really solid and doesn’t
flex like other cheaper Windows laptops do.

00:01:23.750 --> 00:01:27.470
One thing we can complain about is that there’s
no notch in the front to help open up the

00:01:27.470 --> 00:01:31.799
laptop, so you kind of have to jam your fingernail
in there to open it up, and the hinge is pretty

00:01:31.799 --> 00:01:34.259
stiff so it’s tough to open with one hand.

00:01:34.259 --> 00:01:38.040
The trackpad is also pretty good for a Windows
laptop, but you definitely won’t get the

00:01:38.040 --> 00:01:43.210
same experience as with one of the newer MacBooks,
which feature the best trackpads in the business.

00:01:43.210 --> 00:01:46.000
But the XPS 13’s trackpad is still above
average, really only getting topped by Huawei’s

00:01:46.000 --> 00:01:47.000
MateBook X Pro and the Razer Blade Stealth.

00:01:47.000 --> 00:01:50.590
One thing that really stands out about the
new XPS 13 is that it packs a total of three

00:01:50.590 --> 00:01:54.799
full-speed USB-C ports, with two of them supporting
full-speed Thunderbolt 3, and the port on

00:01:54.799 --> 00:01:55.799
the right side has now been upgraded to USB
3 gen 1 which is twice as fast as last year.

00:01:55.799 --> 00:01:59.539
A lot of other Windows laptops only come with
just one Thunderbolt 3 port or two slower

00:01:59.539 --> 00:02:02.229
ones, so having two full-speed ports is impressive.

00:02:02.229 --> 00:02:06.969
It also packs a mini-SD card slot, a headphone
jack, and a neat little battery indicator

00:02:06.969 --> 00:02:08.810
button that shows you the current battery
life.

00:02:08.810 --> 00:02:12.460
One thing that still disappoints us year over
year is the speaker quality.

00:02:12.460 --> 00:02:28.610
It sounds okay but it definitely lacks volume
and a wide range of frequency reproduction.

00:02:28.610 --> 00:02:32.610
A few years ago, these types of speakers were
the norm, but many windows laptops have been

00:02:32.610 --> 00:02:34.150
making big improvements.

00:02:34.150 --> 00:02:38.530
The 720P webcam actually isn’t too bad,
using noise reduction to make for a clear

00:02:38.530 --> 00:02:42.370
but not as sharp image, but the microphone
quality was really terrible.

00:02:42.370 --> 00:02:49.840
Just listen for yourself.

00:02:49.840 --> 00:02:54.120
On the plus side, battery life is also really
impressive compared to last year, but that’s

00:02:54.120 --> 00:02:56.260
using the default battery saving settings.

00:02:56.260 --> 00:03:00.040
If you leave it on these settings, you’ll
get decent performance similar to base 13”

00:03:00.040 --> 00:03:04.440
dual-core MacBook Pro, which is not what you’d
expect from its i5 quad-core processor.

00:03:04.440 --> 00:03:09.180
But if you turn on best performance mode,
you’ll gain a lot of extra processing power.

00:03:09.180 --> 00:03:11.890
And we saw the same results for the graphics
as well.

00:03:11.890 --> 00:03:14.970
Compared to last year, we’re getting a ton
of graphics performance.

00:03:14.970 --> 00:03:17.520
This is probably one of the biggest standout
features of the laptop.

00:03:17.520 --> 00:03:21.490
It’s really powerful for the price, so it
can handle things like entry-level video or

00:03:21.490 --> 00:03:25.320
photo editing really well, and you can handle
simple 4K video editing.

00:03:25.320 --> 00:03:30.120
However, we’re a bit disappointed with the
NVMe storage speed, it’s not too bad, but

00:03:30.120 --> 00:03:32.230
we really hope it’ll speed up next year.

00:03:32.230 --> 00:03:35.540
But either way, If you’re someone who’s
looking for a good quality laptop with great

00:03:35.540 --> 00:03:39.960
performance for around the $1000 range, the
Dell XPS 13 is a good choice.

00:03:39.960 --> 00:03:43.980
It’s a great laptop overall with only a
couple of downsides that many regular users

00:03:43.980 --> 00:03:48.890
may not mind, and at a price of just $1150,
it’s a really good value.

00:03:48.890 --> 00:03:52.230
If you’re someone that will be using the
laptop in bright environments or watching

00:03:52.230 --> 00:03:55.420
a lot of video content and music, you might
want to look elsewere.

00:03:55.420 --> 00:03:59.730
The Huawei Matebook Pro X would be a great
alternative but with everything that has been

00:03:59.730 --> 00:04:02.400
going on with Huawei recently, its a tough
sell.

00:04:02.400 --> 00:04:07.310
If you've got some extra cash, definitely
look into the 4K model of the XPS 13, or maybe

00:04:07.310 --> 00:04:13.090
even one of the higher-end XPS 15 models which
pack dedicated graphics and six-core processors.

00:04:13.090 --> 00:04:16.090
If you’re also considering buying an Apple
MacBook, you should definitely check out our

00:04:16.090 --> 00:04:19.549
comparison between the XPS 13 and the base
13” MacBook Pro.

00:04:19.549 --> 00:04:22.970
If you enjoyed this review, tap the like button
and click the circle above to subscribe.

00:04:22.970 --> 00:04:28.290
Thanks for watching, and we’ll see you in
the next video!

